/*!

\page arcstk-calc

\brief Calculate AccurateRip checksums locally

\version @PROJECT_VERSION@



\section calc_syno SYNOPSIS

arcstk-calc [OPTIONS] AUDIOFILE1 AUDIOFILE2 ...


\section calc_desc DESCRIPTION

Calculates AccurateRip checksums from losslessly encoded audiofiles and
ToC information.

\snippet{doc} include/text_calcdesc.dox TEXT_CALCDESC


\section calc_opts OPTIONS

\subsection calc_input Options for processing input

\par \--first
Declare the first audiofile passed as first track of an album. This option is
implied in \b -m. This switch is intended for cases in which all tracks of an
album are represented as single files but no ToC metadata is present.
See also \b --last and \b --album.

\par \--last
Declare the last audiofile passed as last track of an album. This option is
implied in \b -m. This switch is intended for cases in which all tracks of an
album are represented as single files but no ToC metadata is present.
See also \b --first and \b --album.

\par \--album
Declare that the audiofiles passed form an album in the order they are passed.
This option implies \b --first and \b --last and is implied in \b -m. This
switch is intended for cases in which all tracks of an album are represented as
single files but no ToC metadata is present.

\snippet{doc} include/option_metafile.dox  OPT_METAFILE


\subsection calc_output Options for output

\snippet{doc} include/option_coldelim.dox          OPT_COLDELIM
\snippet{doc} include/option_nofilenames.dox       OPT_NOFILENAMES
\snippet{doc} include/option_nolabels.dox          OPT_NOLABELS
\snippet{doc} include/option_nolengths.dox         OPT_NOLENGTHS
\snippet{doc} include/option_nooffsets.dox         OPT_NOOFFSETS
\snippet{doc} include/option_notracknos.dox        OPT_NOTRACKNOS

\snippet{doc} include/option_help.dox              OPT_HELP

\par \--no-v1
Do not output ARCSv1. By default, the tool outputs both ARCSv1 and ARCSv2.
Since the ARCSv1 checksum is a subtotal of the ARCSv2 checksum, ARCSv1 must
effectively be calculated when ARCSv2 is requested. Therefore, this switch will
not reduce the time required to calculate ARCSv2. Combining this switch with
\b --no-v2 will result in doing nothing.

\par \--no-v2
Do not calculate and output ARCSv2. By default, the tool calculates and outputs
both ARCSv1 and ARCSv2. By specifying \b --no-v2, the calculation and output
of ARCSv2 is suppressed, which should be faster than the default setting.
Combining this switch with \b --no-v1 will result in doing nothing.

\par \--print-id
Print the calculated AccurateRip id. Affects album input only. If \b --print-url
is also specified, the id will be printed before the url.

\par \--print-sums-only
Abbreviates the combination of \b --no-labels, \b --no-track-nos,
\b --no-filenames, \b --no-offsets, and \b --no-lengths. Prints the checksums
and nothing else. If the output contains two columns (or two lines when
specifying \b --tracks-as-cols) the left output column (or first line) will show
ARCSv1 while the right output column (or second line) will show ARCSv2.
This option can be combined with \b --print-id or \b --print-url (if applicable
for the input). In these cases, id or url are both always printed before the
checksums.

\par \--print-url
Print the calculated AccurateRip url. Affects album input only. If \b --print-id
is also specified, the id will be printed before the url.

\par \--tracks-as-cols
Print tracks or filenames as column headers instead of as row labels. This
option implies \b --no-filenames. Columns are ordered left to right according to
the input filenames. If columns represent tracks instead of files, they are
ordered left to right by ascending track number.

\snippet{doc} include/option_listaudioformats.dox  OPT_LISTAUDIOFORMATS

\snippet{doc} include/option_listtocformats.dox    OPT_LISTTOCFORMATS

\snippet{doc} include/option_parser.dox    OPT_PARSER

\snippet{doc} include/option_reader.dox    OPT_READER

\snippet{doc} include/option_logfile.dox   OPT_LOGFILE

\snippet{doc} include/option_outfile.dox   OPT_OUTFILE

\snippet{doc} include/option_quiet.dox     OPT_QUIET

\snippet{doc} include/option_verbosity.dox OPT_VERBOSITY

\snippet{doc} include/option_version.dox   OPT_VERSION


\section calc_exmp Examples

\subsection calc_ALBUMTOCM 1. Album + ToC, using the audio files specified in the ToC

You have: An album ripped to a single audio file, say fLaC, or a set of files
and the ToC as a Cuesheet. The Cuesheet specifies the actual audiofiles, may it
be a single file or one file per track.

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc -m myalbum/toc.cue\endcode


\subsection calc_ALBUMTOCF 2. Album + ToC, overriding the files in the ToC, if any


\subsubsection singlefile Single audio file

You have: An album ripped to a single audio file, say fLaC, and the ToC as a
Cuesheet. The Cuesheet specifies audio files, but you want to override them with
\c myalbum/album_rip.flac instead.

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc -m myalbum/toc.cue myalbum/album_rip.flac\endcode


\subsubsection multifile One audio file per track

You have: An album ripped one-file-per-track to a set of fLaC files, and the ToC
as a Cuesheet. The Cuesheet is stored elsewhere or references WAV files, so you
want to override its file references.

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc -m myalbum/toc.cue myalbum/track_1.flac myalbum/track_2.flac ...\endcode


\subsection calc_ALBUMFILES 3. Audiofiles forming an album, but no ToC

You have: A set of audio files that you know to form an album, but there is no
ToC information. The filenames are such that the first filename is also the
first track and the last filename is the last track of the album.

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc --album myalbum/track_1.flac myalbum/track_2.flac ...\endcode


\subsection calc_FILES 4. Some audiofiles but no ToC

You have: A set of audiofiles that do not form an album. (Either the album is
missing some tracks or the tracks you intend to pass are completely unrelated.)


\subsubsection unknown1 Unrelated intermediate tracks or nothing known

The following just applies the AccurateRip algorithm for \e intermediate tracks
(i.e. that are neither first nor last track) to any input file:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc myalbum/\*.flac\endcode

Of course you can specifiy the order of the filenames explicitly:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc myalbum/f1.flac myalbum/f2.flac ...\endcode


\subsubsection incomplete1 First or last track known but album incomplete

For each call you may or may not specify exactly one first and one last track.
These correspond with the first and last of the audio filenames you pass, but
only if the switches \b --first or \b --last explicitly declare that either
first or last position in the audio filename list should be treated
specifically.

If you know that \c f1.flac is the first track, pass the file as first of
the audio files and declare it accordingly:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc --first myalbum/f1.flac myalbum/f2.flac ...\endcode

If you know that \c f17.flac is the last track, pass the file as last of the
audio files and declare it accordingly:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-calc --last myalbum/f1.flac myalbum/f12.flac ... myalbum/f17.flac\endcode


